  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southeast Asia and Australia Government to Government Partnerships Program (SEAG2G)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Southeast Asia and Australia Government-to-Government Partnerships program (SEAG2G) is an Australian whole-of-government initiative to deepen institutional partnerships between Australia and Southeast Asian countries. It will support Australian government agencies to build and sustain partnerships with counterparts in the region in areas of mutual interest in support of economic and social development. It aims to achieve two outcomes: one to develop broader and deeper partnerships between Australia and Southeast Asia government institutions, and another to improve policy and practice identified through those partnerships.  SEAG2G will work across four priority themes: climate change and energy transition; education and skills; sustainable agriculture and food security; and effective and inclusive public institutions. Southeast Asian nations currently eligible to participate in the program are: Cambodia, Indonesia, Lao PDR, Malaysia, Philippines, Thailand, Timor-Leste, and Vietnam.</narrative>
  </description>
